---
code: authored-decline-class-unreadable
when-fires: a verdict arm emits a report line whose `<verb> <class>` header is NOT readable statically - a dynamic format or an unrecognized class token. lint/source_oracle_solo.rs. No params.
why: AID-NEEDS:law-codes-vary-by-world-not-grammar - the sibling of authored-decline-class, split by WORLD-STATE (the class resolves only at runtime) rather than by a template hole. 27W:rul-report-noise-tolerant: an unrecognized header degrades to a note, never an error.
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- authored-decline-class-unreadable && mise run loom:promote -- authored-decline-class-unreadable`; prove it stuck with `mise run test`, which is also what catches anything else the promotion moved. `mise run loom:vars -- --all authored-decline-class-unreadable` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
---
-- oracle.sh --
# dorc-lang/v0.2
foo__is_converged() {
   case "$1" in
   key) printf 'decline %s cascade not modeled\n' "$2" >>"${DREP_V1:-/dev/null}"
        return 2 ;;
   *) return 2 ;;
   esac
}

-- replay --
$ dorc lint oracle.sh --no-tools
dorc lint findings (advisory; the machine format `--format=jsonl` is the stable surface):

oracle.sh:
  4:9 info [oracle-declined-inventory:authored-decline-class-unreadable] this verdict arm deliberately declines to answer, but its class is not statically readable (a dynamic format string, or an unrecognized class token): matched sites are left to run and the class is only picked up at runtime; a literal, recognized token would make it readable here.

